{"availability":"available","full":"joostone-ahn/ursp-rule-analyzer-releases","name":"ursp-rule-analyzer-releases","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Lua","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-12T14:55:35Z","updated":"2026-06-15T17:53:42Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://github.com/joostone-ahn/ursp-rule-analyzer","topics":[],"demo":"https://ursp-rule-analyzer.onrender.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:33.220Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:33.220Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:33.220Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:33.220Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A powerful web-based tool for analyzing URSP (UE Route Selection Policy) rules used in 5G network slicing. Built to assist engineers interpreting protocol logs or provisioning rules on real devices.","E2E testing of 5G network slicing requires PCF, AMF, SMF, and gNB to be ready simultaneously. In practice, infrastructure readiness varies across entities, making immediate testing difficult.","With a Rel.16+ SIM card, you can provision URSP rules directly onto the device and validate slice routing without waiting for core network readiness. The UE applies rules from EFURSP locally."],"features":["Encode — Build URSP rules visually → generate SIM + NAS hex → write to SIM for immediate device testing","Decode — Paste hex from SIM dumps or NAS traces → get byte-level protocol breakdown (covers URSP rule details that Wireshark doesn't fully decode)","Cross-validate — Compare your PCF/5GC implementation output against this spec-based reference","Encoder — Build URSP rules via GUI and generate hex for SIM provisioning or NAS messages","Decoder — Paste hex from network traces, SIM dumps, or protocol captures to decode instantly"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joostone-ahn/ursp-rule-analyzer-releases/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cc18846b6db3d1492